Efficiency finder report — 3 candidates found (checked and rejected: framer-motion in checkout.tsx is free since `PageTransition` already loads vendor-motion eagerly for all routes; App.tsx preload is correctly gated on merchant auth and idle-paced; sw.js cache-first on hashed assets is an optimization, not waste; mock-api costs are dev-only).

```json
[
  {
    "file": "server/routes.ts",
    "line": 6078,
    "summary": "Resolve endpoint's new schedule/quote lookups run as a second serial DB roundtrip instead of joining the existing Promise.all",
    "failure_scenario": "Every checkout page load for a property invoice with a scheduleId (or trades invoice with a quoteId) now takes merchant/party roundtrip + a second awaited roundtrip before responding, adding one full DB latency (~10-50ms on Neon) to a latency-sensitive public endpoint. Cheaper: the schedule/quote lookups depend only on `invoice`, which is available before the existing `Promise.all([getMerchant, getCheckoutParty])` — add them as third/fourth members of that same Promise.all."
  },
  {
    "file": "client/src/pages/checkout.tsx",
    "line": 189,
    "summary": "Quote useQuery uses default staleTime 0 + refetchOnWindowFocus, refetching an immutable quote (3-4 server DB queries) on every tab refocus",
    "failure_scenario": "A customer on a phone backgrounds and refocuses the payment tab several times; each refocus refires GET /api/trades/quotes/token/:token, which runs quote + client + merchant (+ invoice list when accepted) DB queries server-side, for data that cannot change while they look at it. Cheaper: add staleTime: Infinity (or refetchOnWindowFocus: false) to the query — post-accept transitions are driven by local state, not refetch."
  },
  {
    "file": "server/storage.ts",
    "line": 3413,
    "summary": "getJobInvoicesByQuote selects every invoice row for the quote and the caller filters/picks one in JS",
    "failure_scenario": "Quote GET for an accepted quote fetches all deposit/balance/full invoice rows (all columns) ordered by createdAt just so routes.ts:6790 can .find() the first non-voided one. Row count is small (typically 1-3) so cost is minor, but the cheaper form is a WHERE quoteId = ? AND status <> 'voided' ... LIMIT 1 in the storage method (or at least a column projection), which also moves the 'latest non-voided wins' rule into one place."
  }
]
```
